{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["כי אהיה עמך — And I will grant you favor in the king's eyes, and you will go to Pharaoh and not fear." "וזה לך האות — And the thing you fear from Pharaoh — 'כי אנכי שלחתיך' — do you not see in the burning bush that I am the emissary of the Holy One, blessed be He? And וזה האות לך — this is the sign for you: it is that you can be confident that I will be with you. And likewise we find with Gideon, that the angel said to him: הלא שלחתיך. And regarding what you say: וכי אוציא את בני ישראל ממצרים — that is: with what argument that I make to Pharaoh will he listen to me to let them go?!" "בהוציאך את העם ממצרים — I am commanding you now." "שתעבדו את האלהים על ההר הזה — And you will bring burnt offerings. And this argument you will be able to make: that they will slaughter to Elohim and he will let them go. And even though here it is not spelled out, at the end it is spelled out: ושמעו לקולך ובאת אתה וזקני ישראל אל מלך מצרים וגו׳. ועתה נלכה נא דרך שלשת ימים במדבר ונזבחה. And so each and every time Moshe would say thus to Pharaoh. And likewise we find with Samuel, when the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded him to anoint David, Samuel said to the Holy One, blessed be He: ושמע שאול והרגני. And the Holy One, blessed be He, says to him: עגלת בקר תקח בידך ואמרת לזבוח לה׳ באתי. So too here, by way of wisdom, He commanded Moshe: בהוציאך וגו׳ — and thus you will be able to say to him. Those who explain other meanings are simply mistaken."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {3 "Final clause: 'מי שמפרשים עניינים אחרים אינם אלא טועים גמורים' rendered as 'Those who explain other meanings are simply mistaken'; the subject of מפרשים is unspecified."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:40:22.083021740Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}